KG42.register("rules-de0e020b6f63c4ddae6afec6",{"id":"27-multiple_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R004","paper":"27-multiple_microgrid_trading","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R004","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market coordinator","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"Neighboring microgrids submit requested purchase quantities to the receiving microgrid, which collects those requests for its local selling-price update. Scope: Distributed coordination at each islanded microgrid trading with neighboring microgrids. Condition: During each iteration of the distributed algorithm. Inter-microgrid selling prices are exchanged among the microgrids as inputs to each microgrid's local coordinating computation. Scope: Distributed coordination at each islanded microgrid trading with neighboring microgrids. Condition: During each iteration, using the current price vector λ[k].","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.local_operator under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator","pricing.inter_area"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g22-e022","v141-b-g24-e024"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E002","source":"pricing.inter_area","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g22-e022","v141-b-g23-e023"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Distributed coordination at each islanded microgrid trading with neighboring microgrids.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g22-e022","v141-b-g23-e023","v141-b-g24-e024"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R004-x001","symbol":"E_{i,j}[k]","meaning":"Energy quantity requested by neighboring microgrid μG-j to buy from the receiving microgrid μG-i at iteration k; the neighbor-specific purchase request collected by μG-i.","kind":"operational","domain":"E_{i,j}[k] ≥ 0 (nonnegative energy quantity)","unit":"MWh","indices":["i","j","k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g22-e022","v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g06-e006"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R004-x002","symbol":"E_i^{(s)}[k]","meaning":"Vector of neighbor-specific requested purchase quantities collected by μG-i, [E_{i,1}[k] ... E_{i,M}[k]]^T, used as the input to μG-i's local selling-price update.","kind":"operational","domain":"E_i^{(s)}[k] ∈ R_{\\ge 0}^{M}, with entries E_{i,j}[k] ≥ 0","unit":"MWh","indices":["i","k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g22-e022","v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g06-e006"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R004-theta001","symbol":"λ[k]","meaning":"Current vector of inter-microgrid selling prices λ_i[k], exchanged among microgrids and held fixed as input to each microgrid's local coordination computation at iteration k.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"λ[k] = [λ_1[k], ..., λ_M[k]]^T"},"unit":"price per energy unit","indices":["k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g22-e022","v141-b-g23-e023","v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g38-e038"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Neighboring microgrids submit requested purchase quantities to the receiving microgrid, which collects those requests for its local selling-price update. Scope: Distributed coordination at each islanded microgrid trading with neighboring microgrids. Condition: During each iteration of the distributed algorithm.","expression":"E_i^{(s)}[k] \\leftarrow \\left[E_{i,1}[k], \\ldots, E_{i,M}[k]\\right]^\\top","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R004-x001","v141-c-R004-x002"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g22-e022","v141-b-g24-e024","v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g02-e006"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Inter-microgrid selling prices are exchanged among the microgrids as inputs to each microgrid's local coordinating computation. Scope: Distributed coordination at each islanded microgrid trading with neighboring microgrids. Condition: During each iteration, using the current price vector λ[k].","expression":"\\{\\lambda_i[k]\\}_{i=1}^{M}\\ \\text{are exchanged};\\quad \\lambda[k]=[\\lambda_1[k],\\ldots,\\lambda_M[k]]^\\top \\text{ is fixed in the local coordination computation at iteration }k.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.inter_area","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R004-theta001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g20-e020","v141-b-g22-e022","v141-b-g23-e023","v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g38-e038"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g20-e020","location":{"location_id":"src-f5dd785b87-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III-A. Decentralizing the Problem","anchor_text":"t at t e set o vecto s { i } ca be ead y de ved ow g set {E(b)i }. Note that vector ς = [eTi AE(s)i ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"where α[k] is a positive step factor. In addition, recall from (2) that the set of vectors {E_i^{(s)}} can be readily derived knowing set {E_i^{(b)}}. Note that vector ς = [e_i^T A E_i^{(s)}[k] - ε_i^{(s)}[k]]_{M×1} is a subgradient of the dual concave function C(λ) in λ = λ[k], i.e., C(λ) ≤ C(λ[k]) + ς^T(λ - λ[k]) ∀λ. Finally, (8) also says that λ_i can be updated at μG-i once vector E_i^{(s)}[k] has been built with inputs E_{i,j}[k] collected from the neighboring μGs."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g22-e022","location":{"location_id":"src-f5dd785b87-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III-A. Decentralizing the Problem","anchor_text":"μG-i initialize λi[0] repeat μGs exchange {λi[k]} sh μG-i computes ε(s)i [k] and E(b)i [k] by solvin","equation_id":"Algorithm 1","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1 Distributed approach μG-i initialize λ_i[0] repeat μGs exchange {λ_i[k]} μG-i computes ε_i^{(s)}[k] and E_i^{(b)}[k] by solving (6) with fixed λ[k] μG-i informs μG-j, j≠i, about the energy it is willing to buy, namely E_{j,i}[k], at the given price λ_j[k] with energy requests E_{i,j}[k] from neighboring μGs, μG-i builds E_i^{(s)}[k] ← [E_{i,1}[k] ... E_{i,M}[k]]^T μG-i computes λ_i[k+1] ← λ_i[k] + α[k](e_i^T A E_i^{(s)}[k] - ε_i^{(s)}[k]) k ← k+1 until convergence condition is verified"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g23-e023","location":{"location_id":"src-f5dd785b87-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III-A. Decentralizing the Problem","anchor_text":", g ining interpretation: Each Lagrange multiplier λi may be under- costood as the price per energy ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Each Lagrange multiplier λ_i may be understood as the price per energy unit requested by μG-i to sell energy to its neighbors. Then, Lagrangian function (7) can be seen as the “net expenditure” (the opposite of the net income) for μG-i, i.e., each μG pays for producing energy, for buying energy, and for transporting the energy it buys. Conversely, the μG is paid for the energy it sells. By solving problem (6), μG-i is thus maximizing its benefit for some given selling (λ_i[k]) and buying (λ_j[k], j≠i) prices per energy unit."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g24-e024","location":{"location_id":"src-f5dd785b87-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III-A. Decentralizing the Problem","anchor_text":", g ining interpretation: Each Lagrange multiplier λi may be under- costood as the price per energy ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"According to this view, updating step (8) is clearing the market, i.e., prices should be modified until, globally, the energy demand matches the energy offer. Note that (8) is an example of the law of demand: If the energy offered by μG-i ε_i^{(s)}[k] is less than all the energy demanded by the neighboring μGs from μG-i, i.e., e_i^T A E_i^{(s)}, then the selling price must increase, and λ_i[k+1] ≥ λ_i[k]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e005","location":{"location_id":"src-f5dd785b87-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III-A. Decentralizing the Problem","anchor_text":"μG-i initialize λi[0] repeat μGs exchange {λi[k]} sh μG-i computes ε(s)i [k] and E(b)i [k] by solvin","equation_id":"Algorithm 1","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1 Distributed approach\n\\mu G-i initialize \\lambda_i[0]\nrepeat\n  \\mu Gs exchange \\{\\lambda_i[k]\\}\n  \\mu G-i computes \\varepsilon^{(s)}_i[k] and E^{(b)}_i[k] by solving (6) with fixed \\lambda[k]\n  \\mu G-i informs \\mu G-j, j \\neq i, about the energy it is willing to buy, namely E_{j,i}[k], at the given price \\lambda_j[k] with energy requests E_{i,j}[k] from neighboring \\mu Gs,\n  \\mu G-i builds E^{(s)}_i[k] \\leftarrow [E_{i,1}[k] \\cdots E_{i,M}[k]]^T\n  \\mu G-i computes \\lambda_i[k+1] \\leftarrow \\lambda_i[k] + \\alpha[k](e_i^T A E^{(s)}_i[k] - \\varepsilon^{(s)}_i[k])\n  k \\leftarrow k+1\nuntil convergence condition is verified"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e006","location":{"location_id":"src-f5dd785b87-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III-A. Decentralizing the Problem","anchor_text":"t at t e set o vecto s { i } ca be ead y de ved ow g set {E(b)i }. Note that vector ς = [eTi AE(s)i ","equation_id":"(2)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In addition, recall from (2) that the set of vectors \\{E^{(s)}_i\\} can be readily derived knowing set \\{E^{(b)}_i\\}. [...] \\lambda_i can be updated at \\mu G-i once vector E^{(s)}_i[k] has been built with inputs E_{i,j}[k] collected from the neighboring \\mu Gs."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g06-e006","location":{"location_id":"src-f5dd785b87-p02-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. System Model","anchor_text":"to sell energy Ei,j to μG j, j̸ i, and to buy energy Ek,i fromrgy μG-k, k̸=i. Then, the energy equil","equation_id":"(2)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"where the two M-dimensional column vectors, i.e., E_i^{(b)} = [E_{1,i} ... E_{M,i}]^T, E_i^{(s)} = [E_{i,1} ... E_{i,M}]^T (2) gather all the energy quantities bought and sold, respectively, by μG-i. In addition, we have introduced adjacency matrix A = [a_{i,j}]_{M×M}, where element a_{i,j} is equal to 1 if there exists a connection from μG-i to μG-j and 0 otherwise. Note that, generally, A may be nonsymmetric, meaning that at least two μGs are allowed to exchange energy in one direction only. By convention, we fix a_{i,i}=0. Moreover, a_{i,j}=0 ⇒ E_{i,j}=0 MWh for all i,j=1,...,M."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g38-e038","location":{"location_id":"src-f5dd785b87-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"III-C. Interpretation and Summary","anchor_text":"It is interesting to note that the optimal solution provided in the previous section has a straightf","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Recall that, at μG-i, the Lagrange multipliers can be interpreted as the unitary selling price (λ_i) and the unitary buying prices from the other μGs, that is {λ_j}, with j≠i. Moreover, derivatives C_i'(·) and γ'(·) are the marginal generation cost and the marginal transportation cost, respectively, that are the linear variation on the cost due to an infinitesimal variation of the generated or transported energy, respectively."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g22-e022","quote":"μG-i informs μG-j, j≠i, about the energy it is willing to buy, namely E_{j,i}[k], at the given price λ_j[k]"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g20-e020","quote":"Finally, (8) also says that λ_i can be updated at μG-i once vector E_i^{(s)}[k] has been built with inputs E_{i,j}[k] collected from the neighboring μGs."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g24-e024","quote":"According to this view, updating step (8) is clearing the market"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g22-e022","quote":"μGs exchange {λ_i[k]} μG-i computes ε_i^{(s)}[k] and E_i^{(b)}[k] by solving (6) with fixed λ[k]"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g23-e023","quote":"Each Lagrange multiplier λ_i may be understood as the price per energy unit requested by μG-i to sell energy to its neighbors."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g20-e020","quote":"Finally, (8) also says that λ_i can be updated at μG-i once vector E_i^{(s)}[k] has been built with inputs E_{i,j}[k] collected from the neighboring μGs."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"6430479a5cce546c12d7da8ee7791a9656cb0e8696327f37ee0fece4acc1554b","applicability":"formalized","reason":"C001 is formalized as the source's collection of neighbor-specific requested purchase quantities E_{i,j}[k] into the vector E_i^{(s)}[k]. C002 is formalized as the exchange of the current price vector λ[k] and its use as a fixed input to local coordination. C.1 left x/theta empty because typed variable objects were outside the graph draft; this patch adds only source-defined λ[k], E_{i,j}[k], and E_i^{(s)}[k], bound to existing nodes/edges. The subsequent local selling-price update equation (8) is not formalized inside this rule because the frozen graph lacks the offered-supply quantity ε_i^{(s)} and an output relation from coordination.local_operator to pricing.inter_area; this is recorded as a revision request. All cited B evidence remains unreviewed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-x001","node_ids":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"E_{i,j}[k] is the neighbor-specific purchase request submitted to and received by μG-i; it is an operational quantity under bidding.demand and enters the local coordinator through the demand-to-local-operator edge E001."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-x002","node_ids":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"E_i^{(s)}[k] is the vector assembled from collected E_{i,j}[k] requests; in this rule it represents the collected neighbor demand requests used by the local coordinator, matching bidding.demand -> coordination.local_operator (E001)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-theta001","node_ids":["pricing.inter_area","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E002"],"rationale":"λ[k] is the inter-microgrid selling-price vector exchanged and held fixed as an input to the local coordinating computation; this matches the pricing.inter_area -> coordination.local_operator edge E002."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","node_ids":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"C001 formalizes the collection of neighbor demand requests E_{i,j}[k] into E_i^{(s)}[k], the demand-request input to the local operator represented by edge E001."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","node_ids":["pricing.inter_area","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E002"],"rationale":"C002 formalizes the exchange of {λ_i[k]} and the use of fixed λ[k] by the local operator, represented by the pricing.inter_area -> coordination.local_operator edge E002."}],"revision_requests":["To formalize the actual local selling-price update equation (8), λ_i[k+1] = λ_i[k] + α[k](e_i^T A E_i^{(s)}[k] − ε_i^{(s)}[k]), inside this rule, C.1 would need to add the offered selling quantity ε_i^{(s)} (or bidding.supply) and a directed relation from coordination.local_operator to pricing.inter_area. The current frozen graph has only pricing.inter_area -> coordination.local_operator. Evidence: v141-b-g19-e019, v141-b-g20-e020, v141-b-g22-e022."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
